-- The caller must supply these exact, same-session references before any
-- dependency observation. The second tuple item is continuity data only.
--
--   rootNodeWitness      = #(exactRootNodeReference, capturedHandle)
--   rootSceneWitness     = #(exactRootSceneReference, capturedHandle)
--   managerTargetWitness = #(exactLayerManagerReferenceTarget, capturedHandle)
--
-- rootNodeWitness[1] must come directly from the rootNode global.
-- rootSceneWitness[1] must come directly from the rootScene global.
-- managerTargetWitness[1] has NO approved source in the supplied evidence.
-- Therefore a missing managerTargetWitness is a hard INCOMPLETE result.

-- PSEUDOCODE ONLY:
--
-- validatePreExistingWitness(witness):
--     require exact tuple shape and non-undefined reference
--     reject known Interface and MixinInterface values, plus all unsupported
--     kinds, before any anim-handle operation; type checks are not identity
--     require current handle of the retained reference == captured handle
--     a roundtrip, if separately calibrated, may only compare its result to
--     the already-retained exact reference; never manufacture or adopt one
--     never use a name or class label as identity
--
-- admitRoots(rootNodeWitness, rootSceneWitness):
--     validatePreExistingWitness(rootNodeWitness)
--     validatePreExistingWitness(rootSceneWitness)
--     require rootNode == rootNodeWitness[1]
--     require rootScene == rootSceneWitness[1]
--     require rootNodeWitness[1] != rootSceneWitness[1]
--
-- admitLayer(nodeWitness, backingWitness, rootNodeWitness,
--            rootSceneWitness, managerTargetWitness):
--     validate all five exact retained reference witnesses
--     reject if managerTargetWitness is absent
--     require a separately authenticated, still-current manager anchor
--     require all relevant reference witnesses pairwise unambiguous
--     require node.layer.layerAsRefTarg == backingWitness[1]
--     read only the bounded typed layer/backing/GI profiles
--     do not call refs.dependents here to discover a manager
--     do not accept a dependency object by name/class/handle
--
-- dependency gate (disabled):
--     current empty-layer observation suggests exact rootScene + exact
--     managerTarget, with optional separately retained member nodes.
--     rootNode remains a required global witness but is not required to be a
--     layer backing dependent in this proposed profile.
--     A separately authorised fresh dependency array, if one is ever read,
--     is compared against pre-existing exact witnesses, never used to obtain
--     them. Require exactly one rootScene and manager, no foreign/duplicates,
--     optional calibrated members only; unexpected rootNode is unsupported.
--     Without a pre-existing exact manager witness, its independent current
--     anchor AND authorised dependency evidence, return INCOMPLETE.
--
-- No construction, mutation, cleanup, save/reset, layer lookup, handle-only
-- recovery, new dependency read, baseline, replay, or acceptance is designed.
